    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Fix it Yourself: Destiny's Sports Page\r\n\r\n*\"I can barely read anything on my page. I wanted it to look bold and dramatic with the team colors, but now the text and the background are basically the same color. I don't understand what went wrong.\"*\r\n\r\nAnother hands-on fix - AI Tutor can explain, but the typing is yours.\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n1. **Diagnose:** Look at the `<style>` block in `index.html`. Compare the `background-color` of `body` with its `color`. Can you spot the problem?\r\n2. **Edit:** Fix it yourself by changing a value or two, so every word is readable. Keep Destiny's team colors: navy blue and gold.\r\n3. **Check:** Look at the preview. Can you read the team history *and* the player list?\r\n\r\n> **Hint:** The `color` rule on `body` sets the text color for everything nested inside it - that's **inheritance**, the same thing the Tag Inspector showed you. Fixing one value in one place can fix the whole page.\r\n\r\nWhen you can read every word on the page, click **Continue**.",
